.TH SIT 1 "2026-10-27" "sit 0.1" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
sit \- suckless IPTV player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sit
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR sources ]
.RI [ url ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sit
lists the live channels, movies and series of an Xtream Codes account,
reads M3U playlists and XMLTV guides, and plays everything through libmpv
in one window. It shows now/next programme information, a guide page with
catch-up, and remembers favorites, recently watched items and resume
positions. Configuration is compiled in; see
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.PP
Without sources it shows a few public test streams. Source files are
tab-separated; see
.BR SOURCES .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-s " sources"
Read sources from
.I sources
instead of the default file.
A missing or unreadable file is an error.
.TP
.I url ...
Add the URLs as a source named
.RB \(lq Command line \(rq.
Each URL is listed as a channel.
.SH SOURCES
One source per line, fields separated by tabs.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
A UTF-8 byte-order mark is accepted.
.PP
Xtream Codes:
.RS
.nf
name	xtream	url	user	pass
.fi
.RE
.PP
M3U playlist, URL or local file:
.RS
.nf
name	m3u	url-or-file	[xmltv-url-or-file]
.fi
.RE
.PP
The optional fourth field is an XMLTV guide, URL or file (plain or
.BR .gz ).
Without it the guide URL is taken from
.B x-tvg-url
or
.B url-tvg
in the
.B #EXTM3U
header.
.PP
Public test streams:
.RS
.nf
name	demo
.fi
.RE
.PP
The default sources file is
.I ~/.config/sit/sources
on Unix and
.I %APPDATA%\(rssit\(rssources
on Windows.
If it does not exist,
.I sources.txt
in the same directory is tried as well.
Without such a file, the
.B sources[]
table in
.I config.h
is used.
Lines that do not match the formats above are skipped with a warning.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Play the selection; pressed again on what is playing, switch to full view.
.TP
.B Esc, Backspace
Back.
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move the selection; in the player, previous/next channel.
.TP
.B k, j
Move the selection up or down.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Switch panes; in the player, seek back or forward 10 seconds.
.TP
.B h, l
Switch panes.
.TP
.B Shift+Left, Shift+Right
Seek back or forward 60 seconds.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move one page.
.TP
.B Home, g
Jump to the top.
.TP
.B End, Shift+g
Jump to the bottom.
.TP
.B Tab
Next tab: Live, Movies, Series, Favorites, Recent.
.TP
.B Shift+Tab
Previous tab.
.TP
.B /, Ctrl+f
Search.
.TP
.B 0\-9
Tune to a channel by its number; type the number and press Enter. Esc cancels.
.TP
.B f
Toggle favorite.
.TP
.B e
Guide for a channel; on the guide, Enter on a past programme plays its
recording.
.TP
.B Space
Pause.
.TP
.B [, ]
Previous or next channel.
.TP
.B a, s
Cycle audio or subtitle track.
.TP
.B -, =, m
Volume down, volume up, mute.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the list.
.TP
.B Alt+1..9
Switch source.
.TP
.B F11, Shift+f
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B x
Stop playback.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sit/sources
Providers, also read as
.I sources.txt
if absent.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sit/
Lists, guides and posters.
Safe to delete.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sit/
Resume positions, favorites and recent.
.PP
On Windows the sources file is
.I %APPDATA%\(rssit\(rssources
(or
.IR sources.txt ),
the cache is
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\(rssit ,
and resume, favorites and recent are in
.IR %APPDATA%\(rssit .
.PP
The
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
and
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
environment variables override the corresponding Unix locations.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit
.I config.h
and recompile.
The first build copies
.I config.def.h
to
.IR config.h ;
delete
.I config.h
to restore the defaults.
Fonts, colours, sizes, keys, mpv options, cache times and compiled-in
sources live there.
.RS
.nf
make
make install
.fi
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
SDL2, libmpv, libcurl, zlib and an OpenGL 3.3 driver.
.PP
Debian, Ubuntu:
.RS
.nf
apt install build-essential pkg-config \(rs
            libsdl2-dev libmpv-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev libgl-dev zlib1g-dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Arch:
.RS
.nf
pacman -S base-devel sdl2 mpv curl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Other systems need a C compiler, make, pkg-config and the development
packages of SDL2, libmpv and libcurl.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
